{
  "about": "The shared terrain fixture (SPEC section 8, the terrain grid; briefs M1-03 and M1-04). tests/shared/terrain_fixture/ holds a synthetic world (world.json: origin E 2600000 / N 1200000, height_offset_m 1000.0, the owner's axes), its terrain and datasets configs, a synthetic 0.5 m source (source.f32) and the expected pipeline output under generated/ (manifest.json, terrain/fixture.json, terrain/fixture.f32), computed by design two independent ways (an exact rational area-weighted mean and the 64-bit window rule; identical bits). The pipeline must reproduce generated/ byte for byte; the game must load it into Terrain3D and read these heights back. Heights are local y = H - height_offset_m, float32; every y below is exactly representable in 32 bits.",
